<title>PHILIPPINES: Petron raises all petroleum prices.</title>
<headline>Petron raises all petroleum prices.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Petron Corp said on Thursday it is raising prices of petroleum products to reflect the depreciation of the peso against the dollar.</p>
<p>In a statement, Petron said the wholesale posted price of premium gasoline will be raised by 49 centavos to 11.89 pesos per litre; unleaded gasoline by 49 centavos to 11.23 pesos and regular gasoline by 40 centavos to 10.44 pesos.</p>
<p>The price adjustments will take effect on August 1.</p>
</text>
